Give GPUI text fields on iOS UIKit's own selection UI with UITextInteraction.

Ported from flutter/flutter engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/darwin/ios/framework/Source/FlutterTextInputPlugin.mm
@ 3.50.1 (ae9b586f34a8443573f82ef57c3bf914a908cbf7): `-[FlutterTextInputView textInteraction]`, its touch
forwarding to the view responder and `textInRange:`'s nil check. Copyright 2014 The Flutter Authors. BSD-3-Clause.

What: while GPUITextInputView is first responder it carries a `UITextInteraction` in editable mode, made as Flutter
makes it, so a focused GPUI field gets what a UITextField has: the caret, tap to place it, double tap for a word,
the selection highlight and handles (drag to extend), the loupe on long press, and UIKit's edit menu (Cut, Copy,
Paste, Delete, Select All, AutoFill; on iOS 16+ UIKit presents it through UIEditMenuInteraction), which calls
patch 0036's actions. It leaves when the view resigns.
- The interaction's gestures go on the text input's own view (its `textInputView`), so the view now covers GPUI's
  view (the window sizes it, autoresizing) instead of a hidden 1-point frame, and is its own `textInputView`.
- `hitTest:withEvent:` claims a touch only while editing and only on the field's text (a closest position) or
  within half of Apple's 44 pt touch target of a selection end (a handle knob); every other touch reaches GPUI's
  view as before. Touches it claims but UIKit's gestures leave are forwarded to GPUI's view (Flutter's
  `touchesBegan:` … `touchesCancelled:`), so the app still sees them; a recognized gesture cancels them.
- `selectionRectsForRange:` falls back to the app's first rect when the app gives no selection rects (UIKit draws
  no highlight or handles without them); one-line fields need nothing more.
- `textInRange:` takes nil (UIKit sends it; Flutter checks too). It panicked in objc2 before.

Why: AGENTS.md "iOS text selection": native `UITextInteraction` on iOS. The behaviour table marks iOS
`TextSelectionControls::Native`, so Parallax's own selection engine is off there and nothing selected text.

Test: the native protocol smoke test checks the interaction comes with the responder and goes with it; patch
0028's table still passes. Checked by hand in Parallax's hello on the iPhone 17 Pro and iPad Pro 11-inch
simulators (iOS 26.5): double tap selects a word with handles and the edit menu, a handle drag extends it, Copy
then Paste replaces a selection, long press shows the loupe, taps outside the field reach GPUI.

Upstream PR: not filed yet.

